1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Add hydrochloric acid to three different things.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,240
A strip of magnesium fizzes.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,200
A few marble chips fizz too.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,800
And sodium hydroxide solution doesn't fizz at all,

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,840
it just gets warm.

6
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,760
Same acid, three different results.

7
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,640
By the end of this video, you'll be

8
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:19,280
able to name every substance here, predict the

9
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:22,720
products of each reaction, and balance the equations.

10
00:00:24,734 --> 00:00:26,173
First, names.

11
00:00:26,454 --> 00:00:29,373
The common inorganic acids we'll name here fall

12
00:00:29,454 --> 00:00:30,493
into two groups.

13
00:00:30,974 --> 00:00:34,413
Binary acids are hydrogen joined to one non-metal,

14
00:00:34,494 --> 00:00:35,453
with no oxygen.

15
00:00:35,934 --> 00:00:39,213
They're named hydro, then the non-metal, then ic

16
00:00:39,374 --> 00:00:39,853
acid.

17
00:00:40,574 --> 00:00:43,373
H C l in water is hydrochloric acid.

18
00:00:43,934 --> 00:00:47,133
H B r is hydrobromic acid, H F

19
00:00:47,294 --> 00:00:50,253
is hydrofluoric acid, and H two S is

20
00:00:50,334 --> 00:00:51,933
hydrosulfuric acid.

21
00:00:52,574 --> 00:00:54,653
As a pure gas, H C l is

22
00:00:54,734 --> 00:00:57,373
just called hydrogen chloride, which is what you

23
00:00:57,427 --> 00:00:58,653
saw in the last video.

24
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:03,866
Oxoacids contain oxygen too, and they're named after

25
00:01:03,907 --> 00:01:05,506
the ion inside them.

26
00:01:05,787 --> 00:01:08,266
If the ion ends in ate, the acid

27
00:01:08,347 --> 00:01:12,826
ends in ic: sulfate gives sulfuric acid, nitrate

28
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:16,906
gives nitric acid, phosphate gives phosphoric acid, and

29
00:01:16,987 --> 00:01:19,306
carbonate gives carbonic acid.

30
00:01:19,627 --> 00:01:22,026
If the ion ends in ite, the acid

31
00:01:22,107 --> 00:01:26,026
ends in ous: sulfite gives sulfurous acid, and

32
00:01:26,107 --> 00:01:27,946
nitrite gives nitrous acid.

33
00:01:28,507 --> 00:01:30,826
Oxoacids never start with hydro.

34
00:01:31,227 --> 00:01:33,946
So H two S O four is sulfuric

35
00:01:34,027 --> 00:01:36,506
acid, not hydrosulfuric acid.

36
00:01:36,987 --> 00:01:39,066
That name belongs to H two S.

37
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:44,266
Bases are named like any ionic compound: metal

38
00:01:44,347 --> 00:01:46,266
first, then the negative ion.

39
00:01:46,747 --> 00:01:50,986
Sodium hydroxide, calcium hydroxide, magnesium hydroxide.

40
00:01:51,627 --> 00:01:53,866
Then there are the bases with no hydroxide

41
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:55,146
that you met last video.

42
00:01:55,627 --> 00:01:59,066
Ammonia, N H three, accepts protons.

43
00:01:59,307 --> 00:02:03,146
Write it as ammonia, not "ammonium hydroxide".

44
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:06,586
And metal carbonates and hydrogen carbonates, like calcium

45
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:10,106
carbonate and sodium hydrogen carbonate, react as bases

46
00:02:10,187 --> 00:02:10,666
too.

47
00:02:12,667 --> 00:02:15,866
Acids and bases each share properties because acids

48
00:02:15,947 --> 00:02:19,066
give away protons and bases take them.

49
00:02:19,147 --> 00:02:22,266
Acids taste sour, like lemon juice and vinegar,

50
00:02:22,307 --> 00:02:24,586
and they turn blue litmus red.

51
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:27,746
They react with reactive metals and with carbonates.

52
00:02:28,027 --> 00:02:31,466
Bases taste bitter, feel slippery, like soap, and

53
00:02:31,547 --> 00:02:33,466
turn red litmus blue.

54
00:02:33,627 --> 00:02:36,586
And acids and bases neutralise each other.

55
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:38,559
Never test taste or feel in the lab,

56
00:02:38,614 --> 00:02:39,546
of course.

57
00:02:39,627 --> 00:02:41,866
How strongly each acid gives up its protons

58
00:02:41,947 --> 00:02:44,346
is a separate idea, with its own video.

59
00:02:46,367 --> 00:02:49,086
Those reactions are where prediction comes in.

60
00:02:49,647 --> 00:02:51,806
Every acid reaction in this video makes a

61
00:02:51,967 --> 00:02:54,846
salt: an ionic compound made of a positive

62
00:02:55,007 --> 00:02:57,486
ion from the other reactant, and the negative

63
00:02:57,647 --> 00:02:58,846
ion left from the acid.

64
00:02:59,407 --> 00:03:01,646
Hydrochloric acid makes chlorides.

65
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:06,286
Sulfuric acid makes sulfates, nitric acid makes nitrates,

66
00:03:06,327 --> 00:03:08,526
and phosphoric acid makes phosphates.

67
00:03:09,007 --> 00:03:11,886
Get the salt's formula from the charges first,

68
00:03:11,967 --> 00:03:13,086
then balance.

69
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:15,820
Pattern one:

70
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:19,340
acid plus a hydroxide gives a salt and

71
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:19,900
water.

72
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:21,580
Why water?

73
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,460
Each hydroxide ion accepts a proton from the

74
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:27,500
acid, and a hydroxide ion plus a proton

75
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,060
is a water molecule.

76
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:31,980
Antacid tablets do this with stomach acid, which

77
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,620
is hydrochloric acid.

78
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:37,340
Magnesium hydroxide has a magnesium two plus ion

79
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,060
and two hydroxides.

80
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,820
Each hydroxide needs a proton, so it takes

81
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,420
two hydrochloric acids.

82
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:47,180
The products: magnesium chloride, M g C l

83
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:49,180
two, and two waters.

84
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,280
Now pattern one with a base that has

85
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:54,840
no hydroxide.

86
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:58,720
Fertiliser factories react ammonia with sulfuric acid to

87
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,240
make ammonium sulfate.

88
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:03,920
Each ammonia molecule accepts a proton and becomes

89
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,360
an ammonium ion.

90
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:08,560
Sulfuric acid can give two protons, so it

91
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:11,360
needs two ammonias, and the salt is two

92
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:13,840
ammonium ions with one sulfate.

93
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,640
And here's the catch: there's no water in

94
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:17,440
the products.

95
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:20,480
With no hydroxide, there's nothing for the proton

96
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:21,760
to turn into water.

97
00:04:23,767 --> 00:04:26,966
Pattern two: acid plus a carbonate gives a

98
00:04:27,047 --> 00:04:29,686
salt, water and carbon dioxide.

99
00:04:30,327 --> 00:04:33,366
The carbonate ion accepts two protons and becomes

100
00:04:33,447 --> 00:04:36,886
carbonic acid, which is unstable and breaks straight

101
00:04:37,007 --> 00:04:38,966
into water and carbon dioxide.

102
00:04:39,207 --> 00:04:40,446
That's the fizz.

103
00:04:40,807 --> 00:04:43,126
Marble is calcium carbonate.

104
00:04:43,207 --> 00:04:46,406
With hydrochloric acid, calcium two plus needs two

105
00:04:46,567 --> 00:04:50,806
chlorides, so two hydrochloric acids give calcium chloride,

106
00:04:51,087 --> 00:04:53,126
water and carbon dioxide.

107
00:04:53,207 --> 00:04:56,246
Hydrogen carbonates, like baking soda, follow the same

108
00:04:56,327 --> 00:04:56,966
pattern.

109
00:04:59,000 --> 00:04:59,800
Pattern three:

110
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:03,080
acid plus a reactive metal gives a salt

111
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,840
and hydrogen gas.

112
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:07,400
This one isn't a proton transfer.

113
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:10,520
The metal atoms give electrons to hydrogen ions,

114
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:13,320
which pair up as hydrogen molecules, and the

115
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:15,480
metal ends up as positive ions in the

116
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,280
salt.

117
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:21,160
Aluminium with hydrochloric acid: aluminium is three plus,

118
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,320
so the salt is A l C l

119
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,120
three.

120
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:27,640
Balancing the hydrogen takes six hydrochloric acids and

121
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:31,800
two aluminiums, making two aluminium chlorides and three

122
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,160
hydrogen molecules.

123
00:05:35,167 --> 00:05:37,886
But only metals above hydrogen in the activity

124
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:41,966
series do this, like magnesium, aluminium, zinc and

125
00:05:42,127 --> 00:05:42,526
iron.

126
00:05:43,087 --> 00:05:46,206
Copper and silver sit below hydrogen, so in

127
00:05:46,247 --> 00:05:49,646
a dilute acid like hydrochloric or sulfuric acid,

128
00:05:49,727 --> 00:05:50,526
nothing happens.

129
00:05:50,847 --> 00:05:52,366
No bubbles, no salt.

130
00:05:52,927 --> 00:05:54,286
And watch the gas formula.

131
00:05:54,767 --> 00:05:58,526
Hydrogen gas is H two, never just H.

132
00:06:00,534 --> 00:06:03,733
Patterns two and three both fizz, so how

133
00:06:03,774 --> 00:06:05,173
do you tell the gases apart?

134
00:06:05,734 --> 00:06:07,813
Bubble the gas through limewater.

135
00:06:08,054 --> 00:06:10,333
Carbon dioxide turns it milky.

136
00:06:10,614 --> 00:06:12,453
Hold a burning splint at the mouth of

137
00:06:12,534 --> 00:06:13,493
the tube.

138
00:06:13,614 --> 00:06:16,053
Hydrogen burns with a squeaky pop.

139
00:06:16,374 --> 00:06:18,533
Carbonate means carbon dioxide.

140
00:06:18,934 --> 00:06:20,613
Metal means hydrogen.

141
00:06:22,634 --> 00:06:24,073
So here's what to remember.

142
00:06:24,474 --> 00:06:27,913
For the salt: the metal, or ammonium, names

143
00:06:27,994 --> 00:06:30,393
the first word, and the acid names the

144
00:06:30,474 --> 00:06:30,953
second.

145
00:06:31,514 --> 00:06:35,193
Magnesium with sulfuric acid makes magnesium sulfate.

146
00:06:35,674 --> 00:06:38,673
For the products: hydroxide, water.

147
00:06:38,954 --> 00:06:41,513
Carbonate, water and carbon dioxide.

148
00:06:41,994 --> 00:06:43,433
Metal, hydrogen.

149
00:06:43,914 --> 00:06:47,193
And for the acid's name: ate becomes ic,

150
00:06:47,274 --> 00:06:48,873
ite becomes ous.

151
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:51,540
Your turn.

152
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:55,700
Write a balanced chemical equation, including states, for

153
00:06:55,740 --> 00:06:58,980
the reaction between dilute nitric acid and solid

154
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:00,460
calcium carbonate.

155
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,100
Pause here to answer.

156
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:16,100
Nitric acid is H N O three, and

157
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:19,700
a carbonate means pattern two: a salt, water

158
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:21,060
and carbon dioxide.

159
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,580
Calcium is two plus and nitrate is one

160
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:28,420
minus, so the salt is calcium nitrate, C

161
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,980
a, N O three in brackets, two.

162
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:33,580
That needs two nitric acids.

163
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,780
If you stopped at the salt and water,

164
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:38,340
you left out the carbon dioxide, the gas

165
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:39,620
that makes the fizz.

166
00:07:41,634 --> 00:07:42,273
Last one.

167
00:07:42,914 --> 00:07:46,433
Zinc granules are added to dilute sulfuric acid.

168
00:07:46,474 --> 00:07:48,833
Copper turnings are added to a separate sample

169
00:07:48,914 --> 00:07:50,513
of the same acid.

170
00:07:50,594 --> 00:07:53,233
Use the activity series provided to predict what

171
00:07:53,314 --> 00:07:55,713
would be observed in each test, and write

172
00:07:55,794 --> 00:07:59,073
a balanced equation for any reaction that occurs.

173
00:07:59,194 --> 00:08:00,353
Pause here to answer.

174
00:08:11,567 --> 00:08:14,326
Zinc is above hydrogen, so it fizzes as

175
00:08:14,367 --> 00:08:18,206
hydrogen gas forms, and the zinc slowly dissolves.

176
00:08:18,527 --> 00:08:21,566
Zinc plus sulfuric acid gives zinc sulfate plus

177
00:08:21,647 --> 00:08:23,406
hydrogen, already balanced.

178
00:08:23,967 --> 00:08:26,766
Copper is below hydrogen, so there's no visible

179
00:08:26,847 --> 00:08:28,846
change, and no equation.

180
00:08:29,087 --> 00:08:32,446
Writing copper plus sulfuric acid gives copper sulfate

181
00:08:32,607 --> 00:08:34,206
and hydrogen is the trap.

182
00:08:34,687 --> 00:08:36,366
That reaction doesn't happen.

183
00:08:38,367 --> 00:08:41,486
So for any acid reaction: name the acid,

184
00:08:41,887 --> 00:08:44,046
spot the pattern, build the salt from the

185
00:08:44,127 --> 00:08:48,046
charges, add water, carbon dioxide or hydrogen as

186
00:08:48,087 --> 00:08:50,286
the pattern says, then balance.

187
00:08:51,327 --> 00:08:54,766
Next: neutralisation gives out heat, and you'll calculate

188
00:08:54,847 --> 00:08:55,486
how much.

189
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:58,940
Here are the key notes.

190
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,100
Pause the video if you need more time

191
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:01,980
to copy them.
